---
description: MVP-focused Prisma and database conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

# Schema

- Use Prisma with PostgreSQL.
- Add models and fields only for the active roadmap feature.
- Include IDs, timestamps, relations, and constraints when the domain requires
  them; do not add fields mechanically.
- Store Shopify identifiers instead of duplicating complete Shopify resources.
- Never duplicate OAuth tokens outside Shopify session storage.

# Tenant Safety

- Every merchant-owned query must include or safely resolve the shop boundary.
- Do not treat a client-provided ID as authorization.
- Add unique constraints for real invariants.

# Queries

- Keep Prisma queries in repositories.
- Select only required fields.
- Use stable pagination for growing lists.
- Avoid N+1 access patterns.
- Add indexes for documented query patterns, then verify plans when data volume
  makes it useful.

# Writes and Migrations

- Use transactions when multiple writes must succeed or fail as one operation.
- Keep migrations focused and review generated SQL.
- Never edit a migration already applied to production.
- Prefer additive migrations and safe backfills for live data.
- Do not create tables for future analytics, AI, advanced billing, media,
  loyalty, referral, or integration features.
- MVP billing may extend Shop with a minimal verified entitlement cache; do not
  add a generic subscription-history or usage-metering system.
